# CraftifAI assignment — project rules

Copy to `.cursor/rules/project.mdc` in the assignment repo. This is prepended to every
request, so it stays short deliberately. Detail belongs in the phase prompts.

## What this is

A senior take-home: a multi-tenant AI control plane. Full brief in `@docs/assignment.md`.

It is graded on invariants, not features. A smaller implementation that holds under
concurrency scores higher than a larger one that works on the happy path. When scope and
correctness compete, correctness wins and the scope gets documented as a deliberate cut.

Every decision has to be defensible out loud afterwards. Explain reasoning in commit
messages and decision records, not in code comments.

## Stack — fixed

TypeScript `strict`, Node.js, React/Next.js, PostgreSQL as the authoritative store,
Redis for rate limits and leases, Docker Compose, versioned SQL migrations.

Forbidden on the production path: hosted identity providers, hosted databases, real
payment providers, hosted queues or caches, public CDNs, any internet-accessible runtime
dependency. Do not add a dependency without saying why first.

## Non-negotiable invariants

Nothing in application-process memory is load-bearing for credit correctness,
idempotency, session revocation, rate limiting, or background-job ownership. Assume two
replicas always. An in-memory map or a process-local mutex protecting anything financial
is a bug, not a simplification.

Every query touching tenant data is organization-scoped, enforced server side. A
cross-tenant read returns not-found, never forbidden — a distinct forbidden response
confirms the resource exists.

No balance write without a ledger entry in the same transaction. Nothing financial is
updated in place in a way that loses history.

No database transaction is held open across an outbound network call.

Model credentials and billing secrets never appear in API responses, frontend state, logs,
or source control. Prompts and completions are not logged by default.

## Working rules

- No `TODO`, no stubbed bodies, no dead endpoints. Unbuilt means absent.
- Concurrency-sensitive code is decided by a database constraint or lock, never by
  check-then-act in application code.
- Tests for credits, idempotency, and concurrency run against real PostgreSQL. Never
  SQLite, never a mocked repository. Deterministic — no fixed sleeps as synchronization.
- Every list endpoint is paginated with a stable cursor. Nothing returns an unbounded set.
- Meaningful incremental commits. Git history is graded.
- State assumptions when the brief is ambiguous, pick the smaller interpretation, and flag
  it. Do not ask, and do not silently expand scope.
- If you realize something you built earlier is wrong, say so directly. Those corrections
  are a required deliverable in `AI_USAGE.md`.

## Commit discipline (Abdullah — standing instruction)

- The commit unit is a logical seam that leaves the repo building with tests green. Not
  per-file, not per-hour, and not a phase dump.
- Every commit message carries the why, naming the invariant or decision where one exists.
  No `wip`, no `fix`, no `update`.
- Red-green where natural: failing test first, then the implementation that makes it pass.
- Corrections are their own commits with plain messages explaining what was wrong and why
  the replacement is better. Each is a candidate for `AI_USAGE.md`.
- Never commit `.env`, secrets, keys, tokens, endpoints, or `node_modules`.
- The phase-end commit is the seal after Abdullah reviews the evidence and says go; mid-phase
  commits remain the norm per the working rules above.
